[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"MySQL Group Replication and Paxos Consensus: A Technical Guide"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"MySQL Group Replication is a plugin that provides a highly available, fault-tolerant replication service for MySQL databases. At its core, it relies on an advanced distributed consensus protocol derived from the Paxos algorithm to ensure strict data consistency across multiple server instances."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding the Role of Paxos in MySQL"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"In a distributed database environment, achieving agreement on the order of transactions among nodes is critical. MySQL Group Replication uses XCom (a Paxos-based group communication system) to establish total order broadcasting. This means every server in the group receives and applies transactions in the exact same sequence."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Atomic Delivery: Transactions are delivered to all servers or none at all."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Total Order: All nodes process transactions in an identical sequence to prevent write conflicts."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Fault Tolerance: The group can continue operating even if a subset of nodes fails, provided a majority quorum is maintained."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Configuration"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before enabling Group Replication, specific server options must be configured in the my.cnf file to ensure proper binary logging, GTID (Global Transaction Identifier) usage, and unique server identification."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"[mysqld]
server_id=1
gtid_mode=ON
enforce_gtid_consistency=ON
master_info_repository=TABLE
relay_log_info_repository=TABLE
binlog_checksum=NONE
log_slave_updates=ON
read_only=ON"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Bootstrapping the Group"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"To initialize the first node in a replication group, load the Group Replication plugin, configure the group seed addresses, and bootstrap the primary instance using SQL commands."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"INSTALL PLUGIN group_replication SONAME 'group_replication.so';
SET GLOBAL group_replication_bootstrap_group=ON;
START GROUP_REPLICATION;
SET GLOBAL group_replication_bootstrap_group=OFF;"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Joining Additional Nodes"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once the seed node is running, subsequent nodes can join the cluster dynamically. Connect to the new MySQL instance and execute the following commands to join the existing group."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"INSTALL PLUGIN group_replication SONAME 'group_replication.so';
CHANGE MASTER TO MASTER_USER='rpl_user', MASTER_PASSWORD='Password123!' FOR CHANNEL 'group_replication_applier';
START GROUP_REPLICATION;"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Monitoring Group Replication Status"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Administrators can check the health and membership of the replication group by querying the performance_schema tables. This provides real-time visibility into node states and Paxos group communication."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"SELECT * FROM performance_schema.replication_group_members;"}]
